      "content": "i hear you on the safety nets, but even with subsidies, some people argue that the sheer speed of it all is fundamentally reckless. they say that if we break the current energy system before the new one is fully stable, the resulting economic instability could actually trigger a populist backlash that ends up destroying all the climate progress we've made. is that a valid concern about political and economic stability, or is that just another way of saying we should prioritize fossil fuels to keep the status quo?",
